IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rra-nouns`
IMPORT `rra-logic`
IMPORT `rra-part1-preliminary`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 -- TESTS for Part 1 (ss 2 and 3).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the provision named beside it, before the assertion was run.

§ `Tests -- the three-valued helpers (no law)`

#ASSERT `every one of these answers is yes` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `every one of these answers is yes` (LIST JUST TRUE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `every one of these answers is yes` (LIST NOTHING, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `every one of these answers is yes` (LIST JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `at least one of these answers is yes` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `at least one of these answers is yes` (LIST JUST FALSE, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `at least one of these answers is yes` (LIST JUST FALSE, JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `at least one of these answers is yes` (LIST NOTHING, JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the opposite of this answer` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the opposite of this answer` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the opposite of this answer` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (Penalty OF 5_000, 6) 5_000 6
#ASSERT NOT (`the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (Penalty OF 5_000, 6) 5_001 6)
#ASSERT NOT (`the fine and the term are within the ceilings` (Penalty OF 5_000, 6) 5_000 7)

§ `Tests -- section 2(1), the definitions`

-- "unless the context otherwise requires"
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the Act's definitions apply` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the Act's definitions apply` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "agreed date" means a date specified for the purposes of section 7C(2)(a) in a consent form.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "agreed date" the date is the agreed date` (Date 1 6 2027) (JUST (Date 1 6 2027)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "agreed date" the date is the agreed date` (Date 2 6 2027) (JUST (Date 1 6 2027)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "agreed date" the date is the agreed date` (Date 1 6 2027) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "approved mediator", "claim referral certificate", "collective agreement", "mediation request", "salary" have the
-- meaning given by another Act; "Commissioner", "Employment Claims Tribunal", "investigating officer", "employment
-- assistance payment", "tripartite guidelines" are defined by "means".  Each answers the fact it is given.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "approved mediator" the person is an approved mediator` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "approved mediator" the person is an approved mediator` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "claim referral certificate" the document is a claim referral certificate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "claim referral certificate" the document is a claim referral certificate` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "collective agreement" the agreement is a collective agreement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "collective agreement" the agreement is a collective agreement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "Commissioner" the person is the Commissioner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "Commissioner" the person is the Commissioner` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employment assistance payment" the sum is an employment assistance payment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employment assistance payment" the sum is an employment assistance payment` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "Employment Claims Tribunal" the body is an Employment Claims Tribunal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "Employment Claims Tribunal" the body is an Employment Claims Tribunal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "investigating officer" the person is an investigating officer` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "investigating officer" the person is an investigating officer` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "mediation request" the request is a mediation request` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "mediation request" the request is a mediation request` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "salary" the sum is salary` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "salary" the sum is salary` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "tripartite guidelines" the guidelines are the tripartite guidelines` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "tripartite guidelines" the guidelines are the tripartite guidelines` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "contract of service": an agreement, written or oral, express or implied, by which one person agrees to employ another
-- as an employee and that other agrees to serve as an employee.  All four ways of making it give the same answer.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "contract of service" the agreement is a contract of service` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "employee" means a person who has entered into or works under a contract of service with an employer.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employee" the person is an employee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employee" the person is an employee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employee" the person is an employee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "employer" means a person who employs another under a contract of service, and includes (a) the Government,
-- (b) a statutory authority, (c) a duly authorised agent or manager of an employer, (d) an owner or manager of a business.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the core and the four limbs the text says only "includes": not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "employer" the person is an employer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- section 2(1), the ages`

-- Born 1 January 1960; prescribed minimum retirement age 63; no retirement age stipulated in the contract.
`an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`an employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS JUST 65
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`an employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 60` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS JUST 60
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`an employee whose contract stipulates exactly the prescribed minimum` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS JUST 63
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

`an employee born on 29 February 1960 with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63` MEANS Employment WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 29 2 1960
    `prescribed minimum retirement age` IS 63
    `retirement age stipulated in the contract of service` IS NOTHING
    `prescribed re-employment age` IS 68

#ASSERT `s 2(1) "prescribed minimum retirement age" the employee's prescribed minimum retirement age` `an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "prescribed re-employment age" the employee's prescribed re-employment age` `an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` EQUALS 68

-- "specified age" means the higher of the prescribed minimum retirement age and the age stipulated in the contract.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` `an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` `an employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` EQUALS 65
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` `an employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 60` EQUALS 63
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "specified age" the employee's specified age` `an employee whose contract stipulates exactly the prescribed minimum` EQUALS 63

-- "re-employment" means employment by the same employer on or after the date the employee attains the specified age
-- (here 1 January 2023 for the age of 63, and 1 January 2025 for the age of 65).
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` `an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` TRUE (Date 31 12 2022) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` `an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` `an employee with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63 and no stipulated age` FALSE (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` `an employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` TRUE (Date 1 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` `an employee whose contract stipulates a retirement age of 65` TRUE (Date 1 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Born on 29 February 1960, the 63rd anniversary is on no date of 2023: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment" the employment is re-employment` `an employee born on 29 February 1960 with a prescribed minimum retirement age of 63` TRUE (Date 1 3 2023) EQUALS NOTHING

-- "re-employment contract": a contract of service, between an eligible employee and an employer, to re-employ.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment contract" the contract is a re-employment contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment contract" the contract is a re-employment contract` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment contract" the contract is a re-employment contract` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment contract" the contract is a re-employment contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "re-employment obligations": the section 7A obligations to re-employ, failing which to offer an employment assistance payment.
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment obligations" the obligations are the re-employment obligations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment obligations" the obligations are the re-employment obligations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(1) "re-employment obligations" the obligations are the re-employment obligations` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 2(2), treated as dismissed`

-- (a) the contract is terminated by the employer, by notice or without notice.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the employee is treated as dismissed by the employer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) the employer retires the employee.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the employee is treated as dismissed by the employer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) the employer requires or causes the employee to retire or resign on the ground of age.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the employee is treated as dismissed by the employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Requiring the employee to resign on a ground other than age is not within (b), on the reading of fork F16.
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the employee is treated as dismissed by the employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2(2) the employee is treated as dismissed by the employer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 3(2), the Commissioner's deputies`

#ASSERT `s 3(2) the act is deemed to have been duly performed or exercised by the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the act is deemed to have been duly performed or exercised by the Commissioner` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the act is deemed to have been duly performed or exercised by the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(2) the act is deemed to have been duly performed or exercised by the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- the context-dependent definitions are asked as inputs`

-- A case outside the encoding: a person who is none of the things the "employer" definition names is not covered, and a
-- 29 February birth has no 63rd-anniversary date (asserted above).  The shapes are the same as in the Part 2 tests.
